788, "like_count": 643, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 17, "retweet_count": 19}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117856960011722930", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Everything swings back and forth. But for years, there's been so much talk about the outoftouchness of the Democratic party. But obviously the this year it was the GOP echo chamber, that a candidate for office would assume no electoral penalty for racist tweets about UT students. https://t.co/uaW5W7gTRC", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2118021929055694942"}, {"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "2026-11-04T16:36:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118019686080327746"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/1muAiKOQ9R", "end": 239, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2118019686080327746/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118019655755259904", "start": 216, "url": "https://t.co/1muAiKOQ9R"}]}, "id": "2118019686080327746", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 6215, "like_count": 33, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 7}, "text": "The US trade deficit in computers and chips (the chips are generally imported in box, generally from Mexico, Vietnam or Taiwan) is quite bigger than the trade deficit in everything else, but it is getting close!\n\n1/ https://t.co/1muAiKOQ9R", "url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2118019686080327746"}, {"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "2026-11-04T16:34:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118019097887908146"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/Mrwi7HqCYY", "end": 171, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2118019097887908146/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118019055944679425", "start": 148, "url": "https://t.co/Mrwi7HqCYY"}, {"display_url": "x.com/jasonfurman/st…", "end": 195, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/jasonfurman/status/2118002043247874107", "start": 172, "url": "https://t.co/xBqurvAANS"}]}, "id": "2118019097887908146", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 4145, "like_count": 13, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 3}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118002043247874107", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "To Jason's point, monthly imports of computers and ships reached an annual pace of over $1 trillion in September (~3% of GDP, and up ~ 2 pp v 2024) https://t.co/Mrwi7HqCYY https://t.co/xBqurvAANS", "url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2118019097887908146"}, {"author_id": "2220183580", "created_at": "2026-11-04T16:20:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118015447534583886"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/TimesRadio/sta…", "end": 201, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/TimesRadio/status/2117925264566927808", "start": 178, "url": "https://t.co/HJjMJYAz9a"}]}, "id": "2118015447534583886", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1965, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117925264566927808", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "'If it can stay uited' is doing a huge amount of work here. James Carville said last night 'the civil war starts Wednesday'. He's almost certainly on the button, as mostly he is https://t.co/HJjMJYAz9a", "url": "https://x.com/georgemagnus1/status/2118015447534583886"}, {"author_id": "917683048782503937", "created_at": "2026-11-04T16:18:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118015144412303640"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/GDP_Center/sta…", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/GDP_Center/status/2117659606050566449", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/anza9wXAvI"}]}, "id": "2118015144412303640", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 47, "impression_count": 10118, "like_count": 73, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 9}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117659606050566449", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "This very interesting paper argues that global imbalances cannot be understood simply as the outcome of independent national saving and investment decisions. The structure of the international monetary and financial system helps shape those decisions, determines how capital flows https://t.co/anza9wXAvI", "url": "https://x.com/michaelxpettis/status/2118015144412303640"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "733647469305864195", "name": "Brad Setser", "username": "Brad_Setser"}, {"id": "497231011", "name": "China Beige Book", "username": "ChinaBeigeBook"}, {"id": "3039504459", "name": "Physical Review Letters", "username": "PhysRevLett"}, {"id": "961132338", "name": "Matthew C. Klein", "username": "M_C_Klein"}, {"id": "702235316812275712", "name": "Guy Berger", "username": "EconBerger"}, {"id": "14096763", "name": "Joe Weisenthal", "username": "TheStalwart"}, {"id": "2961589380", "name": "Liz Ann Sonders", "username": "LizAnnSonders"}, {"id": "917683048782503937", "name": "Michael Pettis", "username": "michaelxpettis"}, {"id": "2220183580", "name": "George Magnus", "username": "georgemagnus1"}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2118080567891615887", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzlyxao0frta1mykli6h02epqg4n1", "oldest_id": "2118015144412303640", "result_count": 25}}
